## 4. HALLUCINATION KILL ARCHITECTURE

### Where LLM Hallucinates Today

| Hallucination Type | Example | Current Defense | Gap |
|-------------------|---------|-----------------|-----|
| **Fabricated metrics** | "Market is $50B" with no source | [CONFABULATION-BAN] rule | Rule is prompt-only, not enforced programmatically |
| **False confidence** | Verdict MOUNTAIN with 0 ground truth | Step 6.45 confidence formula | Formula counts agents_fired, not evidence quality |
| **Invented personas** | Do Duc Quang (fabricated person) | [FABRICATION] learned rule | Only catches after the fact, no pre-check |
| **Consensus hallucination** | 5 personas all agree on wrong answer | Red-team gate (Step 7.5) | Red-team is ALSO LLM — hallucinator checking hallucinator |
| **Stale facts presented as current** | "Commission rates are 9%" (was 2020) | No defense | Nothing checks fact freshness |
| **Mechanism-free claims** | "This has a moat" without explaining how | [MOAT-CHECK] rule | Prompt-only, not structural |

### Defense Architecture

```
Level 1: STRUCTURAL (before LLM runs)
├── Local KB provides FLOOR — LLM can ADD but can't contradict verified facts
├── Every claim must be JSON with source+date — prose rejected
├── Pre-loaded base rates per domain — LLM can't claim "90% success" when base rate is 20%
└── Founder constraints loaded — LLM can't recommend impossible paths

Level 2: REAL-TIME (during LLM run)
├── Agent outputs parsed for [?] tags — uncited claims quarantined
├── Cross-agent contradiction detector — flags disagreements immediately
├── Magnitude checks — claim exceeds 3σ from KB mean? → FLAG
└── Source verification — URL mentioned? → WebFetch to confirm

Level 3: POST-HOC (after LLM run, before user sees)
├── Mountain Test (Step 6) — deterministic, no LLM
├── Confidence gate (Step 6.45) — hard formula, no LLM
├── Quality score (stage0-quality-score.py) — deterministic checks
├── KB delta check — "did LLM add any fact that contradicts our KB?" → FLAG
└── Anti-orthodox gate — "is this generic advice any MBA could give?" → REWRITE

Level 4: EVOLUTIONARY (over time)
├── Outcome tracking — "LLM said MOUNTAIN, reality was KILL" → retrain
├── Per-persona accuracy — "Naval consistently overrates moats" → weight down
├── Domain accuracy — "System is 90% right on SaaS, 40% on crypto" → flag weak domains
└── Brier score tracking — calibration over 50+ predictions
```

